Rules-Requires-Root: no
X-Build-Environment: This package wraps a pre-built flagtree-cpu wheel into a
 .deb. The wheel is produced in a container (see
 packaging/debian/build-helpers/Dockerfile.deb) which provides the prebuilt
 LLVM, CMake and Ninja the Triton build needs. The Build-Depends above are
 only what dpkg-buildpackage needs to assemble the .deb after the wheel is
 built.

Package: python3-flagtree-cpu
Architecture: any
Depends: ${python:Depends},
         ${shlibs:Depends},
         ${misc:Depends},
         g++,
         python3-dev
# g++ and python3-dev are runtime dependencies: the CPU backend compiles a
# C++/OpenMP kernel launcher against Python.h at the first kernel launch.
# python3-torch is intentionally NOT declared: users pick the torch build
# that matches their stack via pip — see packaging/INSTALL.md.
Recommends: python3-numpy
Provides: python3-flagtree, python3-triton
Conflicts: python3-triton, python3-flagtree-nvidia, python3-flagtree-iluvatar,
           python3-flagtree-mthreads, python3-flagtree-metax, python3-flagtree-amd,
           python3-flagtree-cambricon, python3-flagtree-hcu, python3-flagtree-xpu
Replaces: python3-triton
Description: FlagTree compiler with CPU backend (Triton-CPU)
 flagtree-cpu is the FlagOS CPU backend for the Triton language, derived from
 triton-lang/triton-cpu. It compiles Triton kernels to native code for the
 host CPU (AArch64 with NEON/SVE2/I8MM, x86-64 with AVX) and runs them
 through OpenMP.
 .
 This package installs into the "triton" Python namespace, like the other
 FlagTree backend packages, and therefore conflicts with them and with the
 upstream python3-triton package. Select the backend at runtime with
 TRITON_CPU_BACKEND=1.
